Fix physmap mappings with non-power-of-two resource sizes.
When address GPIO windowing is not used, preserve the exact memory-resource
size instead of rounding it down to the next lower power of two.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Juan Schroeder <jcschroeder@gmail.com>

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/maps/physmap-core.c b/drivers/mtd/maps/physmap-core.c
index 96eb2e782c38..269a792f0f11 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/maps/physmap-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/maps/physmap-core.c
@@ -519,9 +519,9 @@ static int physmap_flash_probe(struct platform_device *dev)
 			info->maps[i].phys = res->start;
 
 		info->win_order = fls64(resource_size(res)) - 1;
-		info->maps[i].size = BIT(info->win_order +
-					 (info->gpios ?
-					  info->gpios->ndescs : 0));
+		info->maps[i].size = info->gpios ?
+				BIT(info->win_order + info->gpios->ndescs) :
+				resource_size(res);
 
 		info->maps[i].map_priv_1 = (unsigned long)dev;
 
